     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is twice the FDA-labeled maximum. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe 1700 mg may be a typo or a total daily dose entered as a per-dose amount. Possible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 1700 mg total per day, divided into doses\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was verified. I'd recommend checking it with the prescriber or pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
